  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>B</p>\n<p>For a cylinder rolling without slipping, the distance traveled is the number of rotations multiplied by the circumference (2πR). The cylinder travels 5.0 m in 5 turns, so the distance for one turn (the circumference) is 5.0 m / 5 = 1.0 m. Setting 2πR = 1.0 m and solving for R gives R = 1.0 / (2π) ≈ 0.159 m, which is approximately 0.16 m. The time information is not required.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A cylinder of radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> rolls without slipping. It travels <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\"></span> metres in <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5\"></span> seconds at a constant speed, completing five full turns.</p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>?</p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.08\\,\\mathrm{m}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.16\\,\\mathrm{m}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.80\\,\\mathrm{m}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.60\\,\\mathrm{m}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
